# DOM and CSS

## Where DOM things live

| Thing | Place |
|---|---|
| Selector strings and class-name constants | the module's `config.js`, published as `_KDB.elements.selectors.<module>` when other code needs them |
| Cognos chrome selectors and "miss" checks | `core/cognosHost/` catalog, in `_KDB.elements.selectors.<group>` |
| Live DOM nodes and jQuery objects | `_KDB.runtime.<owner>.domRefs` or local variables for one render |
| Listener, observer and AbortController records | `_KDB.runtime.<owner>` buckets (see `runtime.mdc`) |

`_KDB.elements` holds selectors only. The keys `_KDB.elements.kdbWidget`, `kdbControl`, `dropboxById`, `dashboardDropboxes`, `closestBoundDropbox` and `launchpadHideSpot` are never assigned anywhere: code that reads them is a dead branch. Remove such reads when you refactor; never add new ones. The extension's own host element is `_KDB.runtime.core.domRefs.renderParentEl` (owned by `KDB.js`).

## Queries

- Query from the smallest known root (the module's mounted root, the widget element). `document.querySelector` or global `$(...)` only for the module's mount root or a documented case (modal portal, drag layer, body class, Cognos chrome lookups through the chrome selectors).
- DOM refs are valid for one render cycle; after a rebuild, resolve them again.

## Views

- Build (detached subtree from a state snapshot), place (attach at the mount point), sync (apply minimal changes on state change). These can be functions in one `view.js`; they do not need separate files.
- Views read state and never write it. Listener bodies are thin: they call `dispatch(...)` or a controller function.
- Bind listeners at mount or first build with `{ signal }` from the owner's AbortController.
- Observers: one shared observer per concern rather than one per instance; observe the narrowest root; debounce work on bursts; disconnect in `destroy`.
- Batch DOM reads before DOM writes in loops to avoid layout thrashing.

## Safety

- Put user and data text in with `textContent` or attributes. `innerHTML` / `insertAdjacentHTML` only with static strings or closed enums.
- `window.open` for generated URLs uses `noopener`; external URLs come from config (`core/config/baseLinks.js`), not inline literals.

## CSS

- Stylesheets live in `KDB3/css/` and load through the ordered list in `core/css/config/cssHrefList.js` (order matters for specificity).
- New classes use kebab-case with the `kdb-` prefix (`kdb-control__header`). Existing `KDB_*` classes stay until a CSS workstream renames them together with their JS uses.
- No new `<style>` injection from feature code; the per-widget scoped text styles in widgetText are the existing exception.
- Avoid `!important` except to override Cognos host styles.
